    {
      "filename": "Plaque on the Fleet St. Pumping Station (20564488450).jpg",
      "title": "File:Plaque on the Fleet St. Pumping Station (20564488450).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/Plaque_on_the_Fleet_St._Pumping_Station_%2820564488450%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plaque_on_the_Fleet_St._Pumping_Station_(20564488450).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "The Fleet St. Pumping Station (which I'd initially thought to be the Ottawa Waterworks) had a tablet on it, which said 'Expanded 1888'. The sign is fairlyself explanatory if viewed in full screen mode. The Fleet Street Pumping Station was built for the Ottawa Water Works in 1874-75, for both fire suppression and domestic water supply. It was enlarged in 1888 and again in 1901.(Ottawa, Canada, June 2015)",
      "dateCreated": "2015-06-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "lebreton-flats-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "f244",
      "mediumPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/lebreton-flats-wp/plaque-on-the-fleet-st-pumping-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/lebreton-flats-wp/plaque-on-the-fleet-st-pumping-small.webp"
    },
    {
      "filename": "Kayaking school is it? (20129879724).jpg",
      "title": "File:Kayaking school is it? (20129879724).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Kayaking_school_is_it%3F_%2820129879724%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kayaking_school_is_it%3F_(20129879724).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "Just across the Fleet St. pumping station we spotted this group lf kayakers doing what appeared to be an obstacle course on the canal. Kayaking school is it, I thought to myself. No, these kayaks and the kayaking are actually part of the Ottawa River Runners (ORR). This is a whitewater kayak and canoe club located on the Ottawa River in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada. The club is located at the Fleet Street Pumping Station tailrace, in the Lebreton Flats area of Ottawa. The whitewater course that the ORR established and maintains is called The Pumphouse. (Ottawa, Canada, June 2015)",
      "dateCreated": "2015-06-01 00:00",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "lebreton-flats-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "f244",
      "mediumPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/lebreton-flats-wp/kayaking-school-is-it-20129879-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/f/2/4/4/lebreton-flats-wp/kayaking-school-is-it-20129879-small.webp"
    },
